# Walk Speed Tuner — environment template.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in for your machine.
# Lines starting with # are comments. Format: KEY=VALUE (no quotes needed,
# even for paths with spaces).
#
# The build scripts dot-source these files in order, with later files
# overriding earlier ones:
#   1. .env         — optional, committed shared defaults (gitignored too,
#                     but available if you want a shared baseline)
#   2. .env.local   — your personal values (gitignored)
#   3. shell env    — variables already set in your PowerShell session win
#                     over both files

# Required unless you cloned vcpkg into ./vcpkg/ next to this file.
# VCPKG_ROOT=C:\path\to\vcpkg

# Optional. Path to vcvarsall.bat. By default, build.ps1 finds it via
# vswhere (latest VS 2022 install with the C++ x64 tools). Set this only
# if you have multiple VS installs or a non-standard location.
# VCVARSALL=C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\2022\Community\VC\Auxiliary\Build\vcvarsall.bat

# Optional. Path to your Skyrim SE/AE install (the folder containing Data/).
# When set at CMake configure time, CMake adds a post-build step that
# copies the DLL directly to Data\SKSE\Plugins\, so each `cmake --build`
# (or `./build.ps1`) deploys to the game.
# SKYRIM_FOLDER=C:\Steam\steamapps\common\Skyrim Special Edition

# Optional. Path to your Mod Organizer 2 mods/ directory. When set,
# deploy.ps1 copies the staged release tree to
# <SKYRIM_MODS_FOLDER>\WalkSpeedTuner\, which appears as a separate mod
# entry in MO2 you can toggle.
# SKYRIM_MODS_FOLDER=C:\path\to\MO2\mods
